---
title: "SD-03 Push with Server Hooks (UML Sequence Diagram)"
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor C as git client
  participant H as smarthttp.Handler
  participant RP as git receive-pack
  participant HK as anvil hook (child process)
  participant IA as Internal API (127.0.0.1)
  participant R as repos.Service
  participant EV as events.Bus
  participant Q as queue

  C->>H: POST /alice/demo.git/git-receive-pack (commands + pack)
  H->>H: authenticate, Require(Write)
  H->>RP: spawn with ANVIL_REPO_ID, ANVIL_PUSHER_ID, ANVIL_PUSH_ID, ANVIL_TRACE_ID, ANVIL_INTERNAL_TOKEN
  RP->>RP: receive and verify objects
  RP->>HK: pre-receive (stdin: old new ref)
  HK->>IA: POST /internal/hooks/pre-receive
  IA->>R: CheckPush(repo, pusher, updates)
  R-->>IA: allowed / denied + message
  IA-->>HK: decision
  alt denied (protected branch, force push, refs/pull)
    HK-->>RP: exit 1, stderr message
    RP-->>H: report-status: rejected
    H-->>C: "remote: <message>" — push rejected
  else allowed
    HK-->>RP: exit 0
    RP->>RP: update refs
    RP->>HK: post-receive
    HK->>IA: POST /internal/hooks/post-receive
    IA->>R: AfterPush(repo, pusher, updates)
    R->>EV: Publish(git.push / git.tag.created)
    EV->>Q: Enqueue(ci.evaluate, pull.sync)
    R-->>IA: messages ("Create a pull request: …")
    IA-->>HK: messages
    HK-->>RP: exit 0
    RP-->>H: report-status ok
    H-->>C: 200 — push complete
  end
